Per-file license breakdown for `open-assets/postprocessing/`:

| File | License | Origin |
| ---- | ------- | ------ |
| `README.md` | MIT (this repo) | Hand-authored by hackathon-prep maintainers |
| `JamKit_BuiltIn_PostProcessing_Profile.asset` (+ `.meta`) | **MIT** (this repo) | Hand-authored; derived from upstream class names (PostProcessProfile / Bloom / ColorGrading / Vignette) but content is original MIT-licensed work. References upstream MonoScript GUIDs from `Unity-Technologies/PostProcessing` (UCL + BSD-3, depending on file). |

The asset references these upstream MonoScript GUIDs (must be resolvable for
the .asset to load — install `com.unity.postprocessing` 3.4.x via UPM):

- `PostProcessProfile` — GUID `8e6292b2c06870d4495f009f912b9600`
- `Bloom` — GUID `48a79b01ea5641d4aa6daa2e23605641`
- `ColorGrading` — GUID `adb84e30e02715445aeb9959894e3b4d`
- `Vignette` — GUID `40b924e2dad56384a8df2a1e111bb675`

Upstream (NOT bundled; install via UPM):

- PostProcessing v2 (PPv2): https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/PostProcessing
  (Unity Companion License v1.4 for the package, BSD-3-Clause for some files;
  MonoScript GUIDs above are stable across 2.x → 3.4.x)